From: mocha port <local>
Subject: [PATCH 0005] init: skip writepid targets of controllers the kernel lacks

Companion to 0004 (legacy cgroup profiles). WritePidToFiles() writes every
"writepid" target of a service and returns on the FIRST failure, so a platform
.rc line like "writepid /dev/stune/foreground/tasks" (or /dev/cpuset/...) makes
the remaining, valid targets of the same service never written - on mocha neither
CONFIG_CPUSETS nor CONFIG_SCHEDTUNE exists, so /dev/stune and /dev/cpuset groups
are plain directories (or absent) and every such service loses its real
/dev/cpuctl/<group>/tasks membership.

Skip targets whose controller is not configured, keep the errors for groups that
are missing on a configured controller, and stop logging "cpuset cgroup
controller is not mounted!" on every service start (it is the normal state of
this kernel). Same idea as the r15 "mocha stock boot configuration" work of the
Abobo7 lineage-17.1 tree, adapted to the A12 service_utils.cpp split.
---
diff --git a/init/service_utils.cpp b/init/service_utils.cpp
index f2383d7a6..1bb8dfa31 100644
--- a/init/service_utils.cpp
+++ b/init/service_utils.cpp
@@ -305,10 +305,23 @@ Result<void> WritePidToFiles(std::vector<std::string>* files) {
             }
         }
     } else {
-        LOG(ERROR) << "cpuset cgroup controller is not mounted!";
+        // No error: el kernel 3.10 de mocha no compila CONFIG_CPUSETS (el mount de
+        // cpuset falla siempre), y en A12 esto se llama en CADA start de servicio.
     }
     std::string pid_str = std::to_string(getpid());
     for (const auto& file : *files) {
+        // Legacy kernels may not implement these optional controllers: skip their
+        // groups instead of failing, otherwise the loop returns here and the real
+        // writepid targets of the same service (e.g. /dev/cpuctl/.../tasks) are
+        // never written. Retain errors for a missing group on a configured
+        // controller.
+        std::string controller_path;
+        if ((StartsWith(file, "/dev/cpuset/") &&
+             !CgroupGetControllerPath("cpuset", &controller_path)) ||
+            (StartsWith(file, "/dev/stune/") &&
+             !CgroupGetControllerPath("schedtune", &controller_path))) {
+            continue;
+        }
         if (!WriteStringToFile(pid_str, file)) {
             return ErrnoError() << "couldn't write " << pid_str << " to " << file;
         }
